The bug was caused by a regression introduced in commit `e44f06065bf20e8d0e4adacff61350ebd36f299e`, where the logic for handling boot IDs suffixed with an offset was broken. Specifically, when a boot ID with an offset was specified using the `--boot=` option, the boot ID was ignored, leading to incorrect behavior in retrieving journal entries. The merging of the functions `journal_find_boot_by_id()` and `journal_find_boot_by_offset()` into `journal_find_boot()` was necessary to restore the intended functionality and ensure that both parameters could be processed correctly together.

